## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates cost-awareness and decision-making capabilities when designing hybrid ML architectures with latency and privacy constraints—not just model accuracy.

## Key Concepts
- **Hybrid inference economics**: On-device versus edge cost trade-offs with intelligent data routing based on sensitivity, latency, and residency requirements.
- **Data residency and governance**: Regional compliance overhead and architecture implications.
- **Operational robustness**: Rollout strategy, drift detection, fault tolerance, and robust go/no-go criteria for production deployment.

## Code Example
```javascript
function npv(rate, flows) {
  let v = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < flows.length; i++) {
    v += flows[i] / Math.pow(1 + rate, i + 1);
  }
  return v;
}
```

This NPV function calculates net present value to evaluate whether the 18-month investment in the hybrid inference architecture yields positive returns and identifies the break-even horizon.

