## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical on-device crypto trade-offs for privacy-focused apps.

## Key Concepts
- On-device key management
- Key rotation cadence
- AES-256-GCM encryption
- Impact on battery, CPU, memory
- Privacy/compliance costs

## Code Example
```javascript
async function encryptNote(note, key) {
  const enc = new TextEncoder();
  const iv = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(12));
  const alg = { name: 'AES-GCM', iv };
  const ciphertext = await crypto.subtle.encrypt(alg, key, enc.encode(note));
  return { iv, ciphertext: new Uint8Array(ciphertext) };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to measure encryption energy impact on mobile?
- How to rotate keys without re-encrypting all notes?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model privacy-preserving analytics, not ML, with real-world trade-offs across storage, compute, energy, and compliance.

## Key Concepts
- Privacy budgets & CRDTs for local aggregation
- Edge-resource constraints and telemetry design
- Compliance costs and regulatory penalties

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple CRDT-like Grow-Only Counter
class GCounter { constructor() { this.counters = new Map(); }
inc(k, v=1){ this.counters.set(k, Math.max((this.counters.get(k)||0)+v,0)); }
merge(other){ for(const [k,v] of other.counters){ this.counters.set(k, Math.max((this.counters.get(k)||0), v)); } }
value(){ let s=0; for(const v of this.counters.values()) s+=v; return s; }
}
```

