## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates understanding of edge cryptography implementation, privacy-preserving design, and business impact analysis in payment systems—skills critical for roles at Cloudflare, Square, and similar fintech companies.

## Key Concepts
- On-device cryptographic verification using Ed25519 and platform crypto APIs
- Key management lifecycle and rotation strategies
- Mobile device constraints: latency, CPU, memory, and energy budgets
- Local telemetry architecture and storage growth patterns
- Regulatory compliance frameworks for payment verification
- Financial modeling with go/no-go criteria and break-even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: verify an Ed25519 signature on-device
async function verifyReceipt(receipt, publicKey) {
  // receipt: { data: ArrayBuffer, signature: ArrayBuffer }
  const isValid = await crypto.subtle.verify(
    'Ed25519',
    publicKey,
    receipt.signature,
    receipt.data
  );
  return isValid;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses a candidate's ability to translate product goals into a financially grounded technical plan, balancing on-device ML costs, user privacy, and rollout risk.

## Key Concepts

- On-device ML cost modeling (energy, memory, inference latency)
- Data transfer savings and network impact
- Privacy controls and regulatory compliance
- OTA update cadence and maintenance costs
- Rollout strategy, drift monitoring, and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-cost model for CBA calculations
function cba(params) {
  const energy = params.inferences * params.energyPerInference;
  const memory = params.modelSize + params.cacheSize;
  const dataSavings = params.uploadSize * params.reductionRate;
  return { energy, memory, dataSavings };
}
```
